# index.html is generated by build.js from src/. Two people editing src/ will
# always "conflict" here, and a three-way text merge of a 2.5 MB single-file
# app is worse than useless: it can leave conflict markers inside the one
# <script> the whole application lives in, which loads as a syntax error and
# shows nothing at all — a blank page with no clue why.
#
# So git is told not to try. On a conflict it keeps the current copy and marks
# the file; the fix is never to edit it by hand but to merge src/ and run
# `node build.js`, which regenerates it and restamps the service worker.
index.html -merge linguist-generated
sw.js       -merge
